Dear HR Department,

I am writing to formally register my complaint regarding my termination from
Acme Corporation, effective April 4, 2026. I was placed on a Performance
Improvement Plan (PIP) on March 15, 2026, and terminated twenty (20) days
later without being given adequate time or resources to meet the stated
improvement objectives.

GRIEVANCE 1 — INSUFFICIENT PIP DURATION

According to the Employee Handbook (v3) and to my understanding of applicable
labor regulations, the minimum permissible PIP duration for a full-time
employee in my role (Senior Analyst, Grade 4) is no fewer than thirty (30)
calendar days. My PIP lasted only 20 days — a clear violation of stated
policy.

GRIEVANCE 2 — PROCEDURAL DEFICIENCIES

I was not provided a written mid-point review as promised verbally by
HR Manager K. Tan during the PIP kick-off meeting on March 15, 2026. The
absence of this review denied me a meaningful opportunity to course-correct.

GRIEVANCE 3 — CONFLICTING HR REPRESENTATIONS

During the March 22, 2026 hearing, HR Manager K. Tan made verbal commitments
regarding the PIP start date and the timeline for evaluation. The automatic
transcript of that meeting does not accurately reflect what was said. I
request that the original audio recording be reviewed as the authoritative
record.

GRIEVANCE 4 — DATA PRIVACY CONCERNS

I believe my personal performance records may have been accessed and discussed
by individuals outside the HR chain of command, in potential violation of
company data privacy policy.

I request a formal investigation into all four grievances and written
acknowledgement of receipt of this complaint within five (5) business days.

Respectfully submitted,
